# Test: ephemeral ze --plugin ze.flowspec-firewall config edit forwards --plugin to its ephemeral daemon and refuses interface backend vpp, while config edit without --plugin commits.
# Question: when no daemon is running and an operator runs `ze --plugin
#           ze.flowspec-firewall config edit <file>` on a `kernel` file, does
#           `startEphemeralDaemon` forward `--plugin ze.flowspec-firewall` to
#           the spawned daemon so committing `interface backend vpp` is blocked
#           at validation with `commit blocked:` and `--plugin
#           ze.flowspec-firewall` while leaving the stored config unchanged,
#           and does the same session without `--plugin` commit cleanly?
#           A unit test checks `ephemeralDaemonArgv` alone; only spawning the
#           real CLI proves the parent process record, child argv, child
#           dispatcher record, and ephemeral SSH editor validator compose end
#           to end.
# VALIDATES: spec-dataplane-compatibility-guard AC-18 (ephemeral editor door, A-16).
# PREVENTS: `ze --plugin ... config edit` dropping `--plugin` when spawning its
#           ephemeral daemon and committing a configuration that `ze --plugin
#           ... start` would refuse.

option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin
option=exclusive:group=flowspec-nft
option=needs-build-tag:value=ze_vpp:state=present
option=timeout:value=60s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture plugin/dataplane-door-ephemeral-editor $PORT2:timeout=60s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: ephemeral config edit with --plugin ze.flowspec-firewall refused commit and kept stored config unchanged
expect=stderr:contains=OK: ephemeral config edit without --plugin committed interface backend vpp
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
